# A salt pulse through a water column
#
# Three cells of pure water. A fourth vessel holds salt water — the
# feed. Push the feed through the column and collect what comes out.
# After three steps at Courant 0.5, the salt has spread through the
# column by the binomial coefficients: the front disperses exactly
# as the theory says.

# v1 is the default beaker — use it as cell 1
add v1 water 100mL

# cells 2 and 3
new
add v2 water 100mL
new
add v3 water 100mL

# the inlet: salt water at the same volume
new
add v4 water 100mL
add v4 NaCl 5g

# an empty receiver for the effluent
new

# push the salt through three steps
transport v1 v2 v3 from v4 to v5 steps 3 courant 0.5

# look at what ended up where
measure v1 balance
measure v2 balance
measure v3 balance
measure v5 balance
